Relay patch 0002: build GhosttyKit's iOS slices again.

Upstream stopped building the full libghostty for iOS on 2026-08-12
(ghostty-org/ghostty#13760, commit 7a171895dd: only libghostty-vt is
still compiled for iOS). The iOS code paths themselves are still there
(the Metal renderer on a UIView, GHOSTTY_PLATFORM_IOS, NullPty), so
this restores what that commit removed from the build: the ios-arm64
and ios-arm64-simulator slices of `-Dxcframework-target=universal`,
their Metal library, and iOS's deployment target. Relay's iOS app
links them.

It also passes -fblocks to translate-c for iOS: Aro turns Blocks on by
itself only for macOS, and the iOS SDK's CoreGraphics headers declare
block typedefs.

And it sizes fonts on iOS as on macOS: font.face.default_dpi was 72 only
on macOS, so iOS (in points, like macOS) got 96 and fonts a third too
large.

Needs Zig's own iOS fix (patches/zig/0001-ios-null-file.patch).

